@@ -24,6 +24,17 @@ The arguments passed to most callbacks are:
 
 where ``item`` is an element of ``obj``, ``index`` is the ``dict`` or ``list`` index, and ``obj`` is the original object being passed in. But not all callbacks support these arguments. Some functions support fewer callback arguments. See :ref:`API Reference <api>` for more details.
 
+When used as iteratees, :func:`pydash.floor`, :func:`pydash.ceil`, and :func:`pydash.round_` receive only the item and use their default precision of ``0``. Use a ``lambda`` or :func:`pydash.partial` to specify a different precision.
+
+
+.. doctest::
+
+    >>> import pydash
+    >>> pydash.count_by([4.3, 6.1, 6.4], pydash.floor)
+    {4.0: 1, 6.0: 2}
+    >>> pydash.map_([4.32, 6.18], pydash.partial(pydash.floor, precision=1))
+    [4.3, 6.1]
+
 
